{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasisCore","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finsupp.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Prod.Lex","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.EquivFin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card"],"declarations":41,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.standardPolytabloid_dominance_order'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.standardPolytabloid_dominance_order'","kind":"theorem","line":825,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L825-L838","doc":"**Verbatim brick-4 target** (a restatement of\n`SpechtTriangularCore.standardPolytabloid_dominance_order`), now **fully\n`sorry`-free** (`dominance_relation_exists` is proved). Layer 1 reduces the\nsupport membership to a column-orbit image; Layer 2 (lever + the proved dominance\nlemma) supplies the dominance bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.exists_order_colStab_decreasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.exists_order_colStab_decreasing","kind":"theorem","line":801,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L801-L822","doc":"**Layer 2 (sorry-free).** Under a suitable `LinearOrder`, every column\npermutation `π ∈ C_t` sends `{t}` to a tabloid `≤ leadTab T = {T}`. The lever\nturns the (now fully proved) partial order `dom` into the `LinearOrder`; the\nproved `dom_colStab` field supplies the inequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.dominance_relation_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.dominance_relation_exists","kind":"theorem","line":787,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L787-L797","doc":"**The dominance partial order exists (sorry-free).** It is the concrete\n`domRel`, whose reflexivity, transitivity, antisymmetry, and decidability are all\n`sorry`-free; the `dom_colStab` field is supplied by the **proved**\n`dominance_colStab_lemma` (Sagan §2.4). Fully sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.dominance_colStab_lemma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.dominance_colStab_lemma","kind":"theorem","line":707,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L707-L785","doc":"**PROVED (sorry-free) — Sagan's dominance lemma (the former single combinatorial\ncore).** For a **standard** tableau `T` with filling `t = sytToTableau T`, every\ncolumn permutation `π ∈ C_t` sends `{t}` to a tabloid `{π•t}` weakly **dominated\nby** `{t}` in the concrete dominance order `domRel`\n(`domCount {π•t} i m ≤ domCount {t} i m` for all `i, m`). This is the combinatorial\nheart of the standard-basis independence proof — Sagan §2.4's dominance lemma.\n\n**Proof.** Reindex the `π`-twisted count by `π` (`card_filter_perm`), then\ndecompose column-by-column (`Finset.card_eq_sum_card_fiberwise` keyed by\n`colPattern t`). Within one column standardness (`col_strict`, packaged as\n`syt_rowPattern_strictMono_in_col`) makes the \"row `≤ i`\" set `D₂` and the \"label\n`< m`\" set `E` two **down-sets of a chain**, hence **nested** (`col_downsets_nested`);\nsince `π` preserves columns (`mem_colStab`), the `π`-image of the twisted column\ncount lands inside `E`, so it is bounded by both `#D₂` and `#E`, hence by\n`#(D₂ ∩ E)` — the untwisted column count (`col_count_le`). Summed over columns this\nis the whole inequality. No `LinearOrder`/`Finsupp` plumbing; all order axioms were\nalready discharged above. The brick-4 independence chain is now sorry-free.\n\n**Why standard `T` (not all tableaux).** The statement is true precisely *because*\n`T` is standard: columns increase downward (`col_strict`), so each column already\nholds its smallest label at the top — `{t}` is the dominance-**maximum** of its\ncolumn orbit, and any `π ∈ C_t` weakly decreases it. Over *arbitrary* `t` the\nclaim is **false** and is even inconsistent with `dom_antisymm`: applying it at\nboth `t` and `t' = π•t` (note `colStab t' = colStab t ∋ π⁻¹`) forces `{π•t} = {t}`,\ni.e. `colStab t ⊆ rowStab t`; with `colStab t ∩ rowStab t = {1}` that gives\n`colStab t = {1}`, false once `μ` has a column of length ≥ 2. (n=2 single column:\nwith standard `t = id`, the swap `π` moves label `0` down from row `0` to row `1`,\ndropping `domCount` at `(i=0,m=1)` from `1` to `0` — `{π•t}` strictly below `{t}`,\nconsistent.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.col_count_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.col_count_le","kind":"theorem","line":629,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L629-L705","doc":"**The abstract per-everything column-count inequality (sorry-free).** Given a\ncolumn function `c`, a row function `f` strictly monotone in the label within each\ncolumn (`hmono`), and a permutation `σ` preserving columns (`hcol`), the\n`σ`-twisted dominance count is `≤` the untwisted one:\n`#{l | (σ l : ℕ) < m ∧ f l ≤ i} ≤ #{l | (l : ℕ) < m ∧ f l ≤ i}`.\nThe only place column structure / standardness is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.col_downsets_nested","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.col_downsets_nested","kind":"theorem","line":595,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L595-L626","doc":"**Two down-sets of a chain are nested.** Inside a fixed column-fiber\n`C = {l | c l = v}`, the \"row `≤ i`\" set `D₂ = {l ∈ C | f l ≤ i}` and the\n\"label `< m`\" set `E = {l ∈ C | (l:ℕ) < m}` satisfy `D₂ ⊆ E ∨ E ⊆ D₂`, using only\nthat `f` is strictly monotone in the label within the column (`hmono`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.card_filter_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.card_filter_perm","kind":"theorem","line":581,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L581-L593","doc":"**Reindexing a filtered cardinality by a permutation.** For a permutation `σ`\nof a fintype and a decidable predicate `p`, `#{l | p (σ l)} = #{l | p l}`\n(substitute `l ↦ σ l`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_rowPattern_strictMono_in_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_rowPattern_strictMono_in_col","kind":"theorem","line":545,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L545-L569","doc":"**The standardness down-set fact.** For `t = sytToTableau T`, two labels in the\nsame column have rows ordered as the labels: `(l₁:ℕ) < (l₂:ℕ)` and same column\n⟹ `rowPattern t l₁ < rowPattern t l₂`. Hence within a column the labels with row\n`≤ i` form an initial segment (down-set) of the labels (in val-order). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.sytToTableau_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.sytToTableau_mem","kind":"theorem","line":539,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L539-L543","doc":"Each cell of `t = sytToTableau T` lies in `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.entry_sytToTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.entry_sytToTableau","kind":"theorem","line":527,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L527-L537","doc":"**The label sitting in a cell of `t = sytToTableau T` is exactly its entry.**\n`t = (cellLabel T)⁻¹`, and `cellLabel T c` has val `entry c.1.1 c.1.2`, so the\ncell `t l` satisfies `entry (t l).1.1 (t l).1.2 = (l : ℕ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_col_row_lt_of_entry_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_col_row_lt_of_entry_lt","kind":"theorem","line":516,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L516-L525","doc":"**Recovering the row order from the entry order, within a column.** If two\ncells of the same column have ordered entries, their rows are ordered the same way\n(strict mono is injective + an order iso onto its image). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_col_entry_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_col_entry_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L508-L514","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_col_entry_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.syt_col_entry_gap","kind":"theorem","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L484-L506","doc":"**Column entries are strictly monotone in the row.** From `col_strict`\n(adjacent cells), by induction on the gap: for two cells of the same column\n`(i₁, j), (i₂, j) ∈ μ` with `i₁ < i₂`, `entry i₁ j < entry i₂ j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":472,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L472-L472","doc":"**the dominance lemma** (Sagan §2.4): for a **standard** tableau `T`, every\ncolumn permutation `π ∈ C_t` of `t = sytToTableau T` weakly decreases the\ntabloid. **Restricted to standard `T` on purpose** — over *all* tableaux this\nfield is inconsistent with `dom_antisymm`: applying it at both `t` and\n`t' = π•t` (note `colStab t' = colStab t ∋ π⁻¹`, `π⁻¹•t' = t`) forces\n`{π•t} = {t}`, i.e. `colStab t ⊆ rowStab t`; with `colStab t ∩ rowStab t = {1}`\nthat gives `colStab t = {1}`, false once `μ` has a column of length ≥ 2.\nStandard `T` is exactly what the downstream support bound needs\n(`exists_order_colStab_decreasing` only applies it at `sytToTableau T`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L462-L462","doc":"antisymmetry: dominance data refines equality of tabloids ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_trans","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L460-L460","doc":"transitivity ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom_refl","kind":"theorem","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L458-L458","doc":"reflexivity ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.domDec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.domDec","kind":"def","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L456-L456","doc":"decidable (needed to feed the lever) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.dom","kind":"def","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L454-L454","doc":"the dominance relation on tabloids ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":452,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L452-L452","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.DominanceData","kind":"structure","line":445,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L445-L474","doc":"**The core's bundled data (Sagan 2.5.2's dominance content).** A reflexive,\ntransitive, antisymmetric relation `dom` on tabloids of shape `μ` such that for\nevery **standard** tableau `T`, each column permutation `π ∈ C_t` of its filling\n`t = sytToTableau T` sends `{t}` to a weakly-dominated tabloid `dom {π•t} {t}`.\n(The `dom_colStab` field is restricted to standard `T`: over *all* tableaux it\nwould contradict `dom_antisymm` — see that field's doc.) From it (plus the lever\n+ Layer 1) the brick-4 target follows `sorry`-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_decidable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_decidable","kind":"instance","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L423-L425","doc":"**Decidability of the dominance relation (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_iff_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_iff_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L408-L421","doc":"The unbounded relation is equivalent to its clamp to a decidable bounded\nquantifier over `[0, n] × [0, n]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_antisymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_antisymm","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L398-L406","doc":"**Antisymmetry (sorry-free).** Mutual domination forces equal counts, hence\n(by `domCount_inj` + `tabloidRowPattern_injective`) equal tabloids. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_trans","kind":"theorem","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L394-L396","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel_refl","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L392-L392","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domRel","kind":"def","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L386-L390","doc":"**The dominance relation on tabloids.** `domRel a b` — \"`a` is dominated by\n`b`\" — holds when every dominance count of `a` is `≤` the corresponding count of\n`b`.  A genuine partial order (refl/trans/antisymm sorry-free below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_clamp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_clamp","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L370-L384","doc":"**Clamp both indices into `[0, n]`.** The counts depend only on\n`min i n`, `min m n`, by saturation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_sat_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_sat_i","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L356-L368","doc":"**Saturation in `i`.** For `i ≥ n` every row index (which is `< n`) is `≤ i`,\nso the count no longer moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_sat_m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_sat_m","kind":"theorem","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L343-L354","doc":"**Saturation in `m`.** For `m ≥ n` every label has val `< m`, so the count\nno longer moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_inj","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L324-L341","doc":"**Counts determine the row pattern (the antisymmetry engine, sorry-free).**\nIf two row patterns have equal dominance counts everywhere, they are equal:\nthe marginals recover, for each label `l₀` and threshold `i`, the bit\n`f l₀ ≤ i`, and a natural is determined by the set of `i` dominating it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_marginal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_marginal","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L318-L322","doc":"**The marginal at a label is the indicator of \"row `≤ i`\".** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.singleton_filter_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.singleton_filter_card","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L295-L316","doc":"The \"val `= l₀`\" filter is the singleton `{l₀}` or empty, by `Fin.val`\ninjectivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount_succ","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L270-L293","doc":"**Marginal decomposition.** Passing from `m` to `m+1` adds the labels with\nval `= m` and row `≤ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.domCount","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L265-L268","doc":"**The dominance count.** `domCount f i m` is the number of the `m` smallest\nlabels whose row (under the pattern `f`) is `≤ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern_lt_nOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern_lt_nOf","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L259-L263","doc":"The row pattern of a tabloid is bounded by `nOf μ` (descends from tableaux). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern_injective","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L223-L231","doc":"**A tabloid is its row pattern (sorry-free).** `tabloidRowPattern` is injective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern_mk","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L220-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.tabloidRowPattern","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L215-L218","doc":"The row pattern of a tabloid (well-defined on the row-equivalence quotient by\n`rowEquiv_iff`): the function sending each label to the row it lives in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.exists_linearOrder_of_partialOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.exists_linearOrder_of_partialOrder","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L162-L206","doc":"**Szpilrajn for `Fintype`s (sorry-free).** A reflexive, transitive,\nantisymmetric relation on a finite type extends to a `LinearOrder` whose `≤`\ncontains the relation. Filled the Mathlib gap (no `Szpilrajn`/`LinearExtension`\nin the pinned toolchain) via the down-set-cardinality + index lexicographic\ntrick. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.support_subset_colStab_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtDominanceCore.support_subset_colStab_image","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtDominanceCore.lean#L126-L151","doc":"**Layer 1 (sorry-free).** Every tabloid in `supp(e_T)` is `{π•t}` for some\ncolumn permutation `π ∈ C_t`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}